# Vercel Web Analytics Installation Report

## Summary
Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the Next.js App Router project.

## Implementation Details

### Package Installation
- Package `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 was already present in package.json
- No additional installation was required
- Used pnpm as the package manager (confirmed by presence of pnpm-lock.yaml)

### Configuration Changes

**Modified File:**
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Root layout file for Next.js App Router

**Changes Made:**
1. Added import statement:
   ```typescript
   import { Analytics } from '@vercel/analytics/next'
   ```

2. Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the `<body>` tag (after the closing `</TRPCProvider>` tag)

### Framework-Specific Implementation
- Used Next.js App Router specific import: `@vercel/analytics/next`
- Placed the Analytics component in the root layout file as per official Vercel documentation
- Component is positioned inside the `<body>` tag to ensure proper tracking across all pages

### Documentation Reference
Installation instructions were fetched from the official Vercel Analytics quickstart guide:
https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart

The implementation follows the exact pattern recommended for Next.js App Router applications.

### Verification
- Build completed successfully with `pnpm run build`
- TypeScript compilation passed without errors
- No new linting errors introduced by the changes
- The Analytics component will automatically start tracking page views once deployed to Vercel

### Next Steps for User
To complete the setup:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel using `vercel deploy` or through the Vercel dashboard
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel project dashboard (Analytics section)
3. Verify tracking is working by checking browser's Network tab for requests to `/<unique-path>/view` after deployment

## Files Modified
- `src/app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component

## Notes
- The package was already installed in the project dependencies, so no package.json changes were needed
- The implementation preserves all existing functionality and component structure
- Analytics tracking will only be active in production when deployed to Vercel
